      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LITTLEMICKEY (1) was beaten less than 5m when resuming then raced parked but stuck on well as runner-up here last week. Should be close to peak fitness now and draws to get every chance so can go one better. BRITTS MATE NZ (4) is in good form with top-four finishes at her last eight starts, including three wins here. Clocked in second over 2040m last week, albeit a fair way off the winner. Her recent form is good enough to take out a race like this. PENNIE PACKER (7) was close up two back then was behind Britts Mate when third from this barrier last start at this venue. Should enjoy a nice trail so expecting another good run. MY PURPLE PATCH (6) missed narrowly at this venue two back and didn't do a bad job when fourth at Albion Park last time out, beaten only 2.6m. Can play a role again.",
